# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Everything here is public by design. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables are inlined
# into the JavaScript bundle at build time, so anything placed here ships to
# every visitor's browser. The service role key MUST NOT appear in this app —
# it bypasses row level security, and this file is the wrong shape of secret
# store for it. It belongs to the API only.

# From your Supabase project: Settings -> API -> Project URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# From your Supabase project: Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon public.
# Public by design: every row it can reach is reachable only through the row
# level security policies in supabase/migrations.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Where the FastAPI service is reachable from the browser and from this app's
# server components. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local sign-in shortcut. Optional, and ignored outside `next dev`.
#
# Set both to skip the Google round trip while driving the app by hand. They
# are the email and password of a REAL Supabase user you create yourself in
# Dashboard -> Authentication -> Users -> Add user, with "Auto Confirm User"
# ticked. Sign-in through this path produces a genuine token, so the API still
# verifies it and row level security still applies — it is a second credential,
# not a way around the first.
#
# `app/auth/dev-login/route.ts` returns 404 unless NODE_ENV is exactly
# `development`, which `next build` and `next start` never set. Leaving these
# filled in cannot enable anything in a deployed build.
#
# Not NEXT_PUBLIC_: neither value is inlined into the browser bundle. Use an
# address you do not use anywhere else, and a password you do not reuse.
DEV_LOGIN_EMAIL=
DEV_LOGIN_PASSWORD=
